* OPA_QUAD (fast): LABELLED FIT, NOT TI'S MODEL.  Single-pole op-amp fitted to the TI TLV9062 macro / datasheet:
*   A0 = 1e5 (100 dB, pole 100 Hz; macro has more; irrelevant in closed loop), GBW = 10 MHz (datasheet), Rout = 100 ohm series (macro Zo ~ 100 ohm),
*   NO output clamp (rail-to-rail swing is never reached by these signals; the run checks node voltages stay inside 0..5 V), Cin = 4 pF (Cic) + 2 pF pad = 6 pF on in+ (M1a design value), no noise, no slew limit
*   (datasheet SR 6.5 V/us >> the 0.5 V/us signals here), Vos = 0.  Cross-checked against the macro in the slice run (summary in the C-tier JSON).
.subckt OPA_QUAD in1p in1n out1 vcc in2p in2n out2 in3p in3n out3 in4p in4n out4 vee
E1 x1 0 in1p in1n 1e5
R1 x1 y1 1k
C1 y1 0 1.5915e-06
Eo1 z1 0 y1 0 1
Ro1 z1 out1 100
Cp1 in1p vee 6p
E2 x2 0 in2p in2n 1e5
R2 x2 y2 1k
C2 y2 0 1.5915e-06
Eo2 z2 0 y2 0 1
Ro2 z2 out2 100
Cp2 in2p vee 6p
E3 x3 0 in3p in3n 1e5
R3 x3 y3 1k
C3 y3 0 1.5915e-06
Eo3 z3 0 y3 0 1
Ro3 z3 out3 100
Cp3 in3p vee 6p
E4 x4 0 in4p in4n 1e5
R4 x4 y4 1k
C4 y4 0 1.5915e-06
Eo4 z4 0 y4 0 1
Ro4 z4 out4 100
Cp4 in4p vee 6p
.ends OPA_QUAD
